---

You can start chatting with the Agent in under a minute. This quick start opens the Agent, sends a prompt with your current project context, and optionally connects Appwrite MCP for live actions.

# Open the Agent {% #open-the-agent %}

1. Sign in to [Appwrite Cloud](https://cloud.appwrite.io).
2. Open any project (or stay on an organization page).
3. Click the **Agent** control in the Console header to open the right-hand panel.

To use the fullscreen experience, go to `/agent` in the Console. Guests see a sign-in prompt before chat is available.

{% info title="Feature availability" %}
If you do not see Agent, confirm you are on Appwrite Cloud and that the AI agent feature is enabled for your Console profile.
{% /info %}

# Ask a question {% #ask-a-question %}

1. Click a suggestion chip, or type a question in the composer (for example `How do I create a new database?`).
2. Send the message.
3. Review the reply. The Agent uses your current organization, project, and page as context.

You can attach files, use voice input where supported, stop a run in progress, retry a failed turn, or edit and resend a previous message. See [Chat with the Agent](/docs/products/agent/chat).

# Connect Appwrite MCP (optional) {% #connect-mcp %}

Connecting [Appwrite MCP](/docs/tooling/ai/mcp-servers/api) lets the Agent list resources and create or update them with your approval.

1. In the Agent panel or at **Agent** > **Settings** > **MCP**, find **Appwrite MCP**.
2. Click **Connect** and complete the OAuth consent for **Appwrite Agent**.
3. Confirm the connection shows **Connected**.

With MCP enabled, try an action prompt such as `List the databases and tables in this project` or `Create a todos table with title and done columns`.

See [Connect Appwrite MCP](/docs/products/agent/connect-mcp) for reconnect and custom servers.

# Next steps {% #next-steps %}

- Add [memory](/docs/products/agent/add-memory) so the Agent remembers preferences across chats.
- Register a [custom model](/docs/products/agent/add-model) if you want to use your own provider keys.
- Schedule recurring checks with [automations](/docs/products/agent/create-automation).
